    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0762" n="642" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg642"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.002 Mussolini/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Garrett</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-03T17:00:00-05:00">February 3, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Embassy’s 9, February 2, 4 p.m. The international aspects of the Butler
                    incident no longer exist. All that remains is for the Navy <pb facs="0763"
                        n="643" xml:id="pg643"/> Department to take disciplinary action. Therefore,
                    we feel that the request of Prime Minister Mussolini is inappropriate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
